<!--Post: 10436--><!--Time: 1109956758-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10436"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lorenap<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lorenap<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 9:19 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The item removed was a citation Dennis Rader had given to this person. It had his signature.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10436-->
<!--Post: 10453--><!--Time: 1109963240-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10453"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Freya<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Freya<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 11:07 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->A few days ago, a person in the chatroom claimed to be selling a animal citation letter Rader had sent to her address. The current bid for it was approx. $130. Also, his business card was selling for over $100. I filed a complaint with Ebay as a seller, as I&#39;m sure thousands of other people did, and I&#39;m very pleased to see that the auctions have been removed. Thanks for starting this thread, Juno! <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10453-->
<!--Post: 10477--><!--Time: 1109969434-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10477"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:linnieskid@earthlink.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Linnieskid<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Linnieskid<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 12:50 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Freya have you been contacted by LE regarding the post, supposedly from BTK, where you were mentioned?  Just curious.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10477-->
<!--Post: 10482--><!--Time: 1109970434-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10482"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 1:07 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->lol that&#39;s funny I had been thowing a fit on ebay, told them I was banning them for poor taste. I bet I wasn&#39;t the only one<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10482-->
<!--Post: 10529--><!--Time: 1109983990-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10529"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lostdog<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lostdog<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 4:53 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Response to your question for item #5562873018 - BTK Psychopathic Killer Word &amp; Number Puzzle <BR> <BR>Dear <a href="mailto:LostDog@eBay.com">LostDog@eBay.com</a> , <BR> <BR>You asked: <BR> <BR>&#34;I’m a HUGE BTK memorabilia collector! <BR>How much for 100 puzzles?  <BR>Can I get a volume discount?&#34; <BR> <BR>LostDog &#40;203&#41; <BR> <BR> <BR>The Seller replies: <BR> <BR>There is only one puzzle. <BR>It is in the form of a .jpg file that I email to a purchaser.  <BR>I just listed the total quantity to be as many as I could handle on one listing.  <BR>Otherwise I would have to restart a new auction whenever one person would buy one. <BR>I hope that makes sense. <BR>If you buy the puzzle, remind me and I will also include other BTK related items in the email that I send to you. <BR>  <BR>One thing of interest, about 2 months ago, I sent a suggestion to the police about BTK after he disclosed that he was a Ham Radio Operator in the 1950&#39;s.  <BR>The police came out and interviewed me and found out about Ham Radio and the callbook that lists all Licensed Operators. <BR>When they were finishing up, they announced that they wanted to do a DNA swab of me.  <BR>It was fine with me, but it made my wife nervous. <BR>I was of the right age profile and had several other similiarities to the profile. <BR> <BR>So if you want to get the one puzzle that BTK made, I invite you to buy for $4.95 delivered. <BR> <BR> <BR>ALL: I was going to write back and ask: How much for a swab? <BR> <BR>Man, I was gonna SLAM this guy right here for all to see. What a hoot that would be!  <BR> <BR>Then eBay shut his auction down and he emailed me the puzzle and other attachments &#40;photos, articles, etc.&#41;… for free. <BR> <BR>Then I thought about this guy and his wife and Witchita… and the world. <BR> <BR>When HBO airs “BTK: Reign of Terror” starring Bud Cort as DCK and John Larroquette as Lt. Landhwer will we denounce it as crass commercialism or Tivo it and call it art? <BR> <BR>When Stone Phillips nails the Deitz interview, will we buy the beer and biscuits that bookend the segment? <BR> <BR>When CNN or FOX props up Steve Relford to ask,  <BR> <BR>“So, what are you going to say to BTK when you face him tomorrow?,”  <BR> <BR>...will we scrutinize his answer or realize how efficiently we are getting sucked into a fetid sinkhole that used to be called Western Civilization. <BR> <BR>Wow,… heavy. <BR> <BR>OK…OF COURSE we’re going to watch. <BR>We’re CatchBTK for corn’s sake. <BR>But MILLIONS will buy the beer and then flip the channel to see how many banana slugs a hot little flight attendant can fit in her mouth! <BR> <BR>Before we judge this guy too harshly, look at eBay guy’s world. <BR> <BR>He knew about ham radios and he called the WPD. <BR>He let a cop stick a QTip in his mouth and his wife got scared. <BR> <BR>Because he was 56 or 59 or 62, the cashier smiled and then… glared at him every time he left with his groceries. <BR> <BR>Everyone in Wichita and beyond is a DCK victim on some level. <BR> <BR>eBay guy didn’t lose a mother or a child to BTK, but he lives in the residue of fear and anguish that sticks to every Wichitan’s shoes.  <BR> <BR>How are you responding to the stimulus? <BR>What little bit of your humanity has been scorched and shed? <BR> <BR>Was eBay guy wrong to try to make a buck off of DCK’s notoriety? <BR> <BR>Yes, and eBay shut him down for it. <BR> <BR>Who’s going to shut down Stone Phillips?&#42; <BR> <BR> <BR>Thinking till it hurts, <BR> <BR>Lost <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR>&#42; If someone is tempted to post that Stone Phillips is a journalist… be warned…  the rest of us are going to laugh at you HARD! <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
